From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] proxy: run the Venus render server in process on macOS

Venus hands Metal heaps (process-local objects) from the render server to
the renderer, so the server must be a thread of QEMU's process, not a
forked one. Build with -Drender-server-worker=thread.

Upstream: not sent (macOS only).
Test: Venus in an app VM (vulkaninfo shows Virtio-GPU Venus).

diff --git a/src/proxy/proxy_renderer.c b/src/proxy/proxy_renderer.c
index 2c2d04b..24784ae 100644
--- a/src/proxy/proxy_renderer.c
+++ b/src/proxy/proxy_renderer.c
@@ -16,6 +16,11 @@ int
 proxy_renderer_init(const struct proxy_renderer_cbs *cbs, uint32_t flags)
 {
    bool in_process = !(flags & VIRGL_RENDERER_RENDER_SERVER);
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(ENABLE_RENDER_SERVER_WORKER_THREAD)
+   /* Metal heaps are process-local: the render server must run as a thread
+    * of this process, so blobs can be mapped into the guest. */
+   in_process = true;
+#endif
 
    assert(flags & VIRGL_RENDERER_NO_VIRGL);
 
